    ],
    "resources": [
      {
        "label": "React Docs – Hooks",
        "href": "https://reactjs.org/docs/hooks-intro.html"
      }
    ]
  },
  "read": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "use-state",
        "title": "Using useState",
        "paragraphs": [
          "useState is the most basic hook for adding state to a functional component. It returns a state variable and a function to update it.",
          "The initial state can be a value or a lazy initializer function."
        ],
        "codeSample": "import React, { useState } from 'react';\n\nfunction Counter() {\n  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>You clicked {count} times</p>\n      <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>Click me</button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default Counter;",
        "callout": "Remember to pass an initial state value or a function that returns the initial state."
      },
      {
        "id": "use-effect-fetch",
        "title": "Fetching Data with useEffect",
        "paragraphs": [
          "useEffect runs after every render by default. To fetch data only once, provide an empty dependency array.",
          "Always clean up side‑effects to avoid memory leaks, especially with async operations."
        ],
        "codeSample": "import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\n\nfunction DataFetcher() {\n  const [data, setData] = useState(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    let isMounted = true;\n    fetch('https://api.example.com/data')\n      .then(res => res.json())\n      .then(json => {\n        if (isMounted) setData(json);\n      });\n    return () => { isMounted = false; };\n  }, []);\n\n  if (!data) return <p>Loading...</p>;\n  return <pre>{JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)}</pre>;\n}\n\nexport default DataFetcher;",
        "callout": "Use the cleanup function to cancel ongoing requests or abort operations."
      },
      {
        "id": "use-effect-cleanup",
        "title": "Cleaning Up Effects",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Effects can add event listeners, timers, or subscriptions. Always return a cleanup function to remove them.",
