        "callout": "The empty dependency array ensures the listener is added only once."
      },
      {
        "id": "use-effect-async",
        "title": "Async Logic Inside useEffect",
        "paragraphs": [
          "You cannot mark the effect callback as async directly. Instead, define an async function inside and invoke it.",
          "This pattern keeps the effect clean and allows error handling."
        ],
        "codeSample": "import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\n\nfunction AsyncEffect() {\n  const [posts, setPosts] = useState([]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const fetchPosts = async () => {\n      const res = await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts');\n      const json = await res.json();\n      setPosts(json);\n    };\n    fetchPosts();\n  }, []);\n\n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {posts.map(p => (\n        <li key={p.id}>{p.title}</li>\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default AsyncEffect;",
